  "body": "### Environment\n- OS: macOS (arm64)\n- Magpie Version: 0.1.1318\n\n### Description\nWhen `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` is set to `~/.omp/agent` in the user's shell environment (which is commonly set by users or plugins migrating from Pi to Oh My Pi), Magpie desktop app and background daemon continuously panic on startup or during session warm-up:\n\n```text\npanic: close of nil channel\n\ngoroutine 102 [running]:\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions.refresh.func5(...)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions/sessions.go:891\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions.refresh({0x4e5a9e1fa000?, 0x3d9, 0x1075b98a0?}, {0x4e5a9e1fa000, 0x3d9, 0x0?})\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions/sessions.go:905 +0xe08\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions.statsIn(0x0, {0xc2ae939f1928f2d0?, 0xbedec890?, 0x1075b98a0?}, 0x4e5a9cc36d50)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions/stats.go:143 +0x430\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions.StatsAndNative(0x0)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions/stats.go:117 +0x68\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui.combinedSessionStats(0x0)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui/sessions.go:466 +0x48\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui.statsFor(0x1045b0340?)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui/sessions.go:443 +0x2ac\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui.warmSessions.func1.1.warmSteps.1()\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui/sessions.go:507 +0x20\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui.warmUp(...)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui/sessions.go:529 +0x38\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui.warmSessions.func1.1()\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gui/sessions.go:497 +0x50\ngithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions.Warm(...)\n\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/sessions/quiet.go:31 +0x94\n```\n\n### Root Cause\n1. In `internal/sessions/pi.go`:\n   `PiDir()` respects `$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. When `$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` points to `~/.omp/agent`, `piFiles()` collects session files under `~/.omp/agent/sessions/`.\n2. In `internal/sessions/omp.go`:\n   `OmpDir()` defaults to `~/.omp/agent`, and `ompFiles()` collects session files from the exact same directory.\n3. In `internal/sessions/sessions.go:allFiles()`:\n   Files from both `piFiles()` and `ompFiles()` are appended together into `out []file` without path deduplication.\n4. In `internal/sessions/sessions.go:refresh()`:\n   Duplicate `f.path` entries are appended into `todo` slice, resulting in multiple concurrent jobs targeting the exact same file path.\n5. In `publish(i int)`:\n   When worker 1 finishes, it runs:\n   ```go\n   close(parsing[j.f.path])\n   delete(parsing, j.f.path)\n   ```\n   When worker 2 finishes for the duplicate file, `parsing[j.f.path]` is `nil`. Closing a nil channel immediately triggers `panic: close of nil channel`.\n6. Furthermore, on macOS desktop launches, `proc.UserPath()` queries the user's interactive login shell (`zsh -ilc`), detects `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, and injects it into Magpie's environment, causing the desktop app to crash even when launched from Finder/Dock.\n\n### Suggested Fix\n1. In `internal/sessions/sessions.go` -> `refresh()`, deduplicate file paths when building `todo`:\n   ```go\n   seen := make(map[string]bool, len(want))\n   for _, f := range want {\n       if f.cold || seen[f.path] {\n           continue\n       }\n       seen[f.path] = true\n       // ...\n   ```\n2. Defensively guard channel closing in `publish()`:\n   ```go\n   if ch := parsing[j.f.path]; ch != nil {\n       close(ch)\n       delete(parsing, j.f.path)\n   }\n   ```",
