     "body": "Found while landing #2932's fix (CodeBuddy Code in WorkBuddy's folder).\n\n#2932's fix keeps each path once in `allFiles` and `callSources` (`distinctPaths`), and reads CodeBuddy Code's folder as WorkBuddy's when `os.SameFile` says the two are one folder. The other pairs of agents that a variable can point at one folder only get the path-text dedup:\n\n- Pi and omp: `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` set to omp's `~/.omp/agent` lists each `sessions/*/*.jsonl` from `piFiles` and `ompFiles`.\n- Qoder and Qoder CN: `QODER_CONFIG_DIR` and `QODERCN_CONFIG_DIR` on one folder lists each file from both `ccFiles` calls.\n\nWhen both spell the folder the same, `distinctPaths` keeps the first listing, so a session is read once (under the first agent's name). When the spellings differ (a symlink or junction, or `C:\\Users\\x\\.qoder` beside `c:\\users\\x\\.qoder` on Windows), the paths differ as text, so each session is listed twice, under both agents, and its calls are counted twice in usage. It no longer crashes: that was the duplicate path in one refresh, fixed in #2932.\n\nNot reproduced with a real install; this is from reading `allFiles`, `piFilesIn`, `ompFilesUnder` and `QoderDir`. A fix would decide the agent for a shared folder as #2932 did for WorkBuddy (`sameFolder` in `internal/sessions/workbuddy.go`), or key the dedup on the file's identity instead of its path text.",
